Here's how to handle each scenario with MSTest:

### 1. Windows-only tests

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]  // custom attribute approach
public void RegistryTest()
{
    if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())
    {
        Assert.Inconclusive("Requires Windows");
        return;
    }
    // registry code here
}
```

Or use a build-time constant:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[System.Runtime.Versioning.SupportedOSPlatform("windows")]
public void RegistryTest() { /* ... */ }
```

### 2. Skip in CI (requires local GPU)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GpuRenderTest()
{
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") == "true")
    {
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI — requires local GPU");
        return;
    }
    // GPU test logic
}
```

Or use a **condition attribute** pattern:

```csharp
[AttributeUsage(AttributeTargets.Method)]
public class SkipInCIAttribute : Attribute { }

// In your test base class, check for it in [TestInitialize]
[TestInitialize]
public void CheckSkipConditions()
{
    var method = GetType().GetMethod(TestContext.TestName!);
    if (method?.GetCustomAttribute<SkipInCIAttribute>() != null
        && Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") == "true")
    {
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI");
    }
}
```

### 3. Flaky external API — retry pattern

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[DataRow(1)]
[DataRow(2)]  // not ideal — use a retry helper instead:
public void WeatherApiTest()
{
    RetryHelper.Execute(maxRetries: 3, delay: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2), () =>
    {
        var result = _weatherClient.GetForecast("Seattle");
        Assert.IsNotNull(result);
    });
}

// Helper
public static class RetryHelper
{
    public static void Execute(int maxRetries, TimeSpan delay, Action action)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < maxRetries; i++)
        {
            try { action(); return; }
            catch when (i < maxRetries - 1)
            {
                Thread.Sleep(delay);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### 4. Cleanup even on failure — use `[TestCleanup]`

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class TempFileTests
{
    private readonly List<string> _tempFiles = new();

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessFileTest()
    {
        var path = Path.GetTempFileName();
        _tempFiles.Add(path);

        File.WriteAllText(path, "test data");
        var result = MyProcessor.Process(path);
        Assert.IsTrue(result.Success);
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        foreach (var file in _tempFiles)
        {
            try { File.Delete(file); } catch { /* best-effort */ }
        }
        _tempFiles.Clear();
    }
}
```

**Summary table:**

| Scenario | Approach |
|---|---|
| OS-specific | Guard with `OperatingSystem.IsWindows()` + `Assert.Inconclusive` |
| Skip in CI | Check `CI` env var in `[TestInitialize]` |
| Flaky API | Retry helper with backoff |
| Cleanup on failure | `[TestCleanup]` — runs regardless of pass/fail |

`Assert.Inconclusive` is key — it marks the test as **skipped** rather than failed, keeping your CI results clean.
